			<div class="content" id="post-content-4331994">
									

<p>So, I'm a sucker for Language of Flowers references, and this is a nice short punchy article with an unexpected format screw, thus you have my +1.</p>
<p>I will say that following the meanings is a bit difficult when there are so many flowers to keep track of. What I would have recommended is that the filenames include both the flower <em>and</em> the &quot;meaning&quot;, so if the reader happens to have forgotten what one meaning was, they could just hover over the image to see its url and not need to search through the entire document for the first footnote. That's just a quality of life edit that might not be entirely necessary, though!</p>

